data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Keep the indices of the waiting readings on a stack, last in first out. For each new reading, pop every waiting\nindex whose value is strictly smaller than the new value. For each popped index, the answer is the new index\nminus that index. Then push the new index. A reading that is still on the stack at the end has no answer, and its\nentry stays 0. Each index is pushed once and popped once, so the total work is O(n)."},"hints_note":null}

